		(property "Description" "Ideal diode (tracker S11U1 part): 1.5-5.5 V, ~110 mOhm at 3 V so the cell loses ~30 mV under a 250 mA burst instead of the 300 mV a Schottky cost, 0.15 uA, turns off when VOUT exceeds VIN by 80 mV. Nothing may ever charge the cell: this is the block. A 12 V fault on VBAT needs the boost high-side and sheet-1 D2 to both fail shorted. SC70-6"
			(at 67.31 41.91 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
